# Native Soma Chat artifact UI in the isolated, fictional fixture. No runners/accounts or real sends.
# Prerequisite: -PartifactPreview :artifact-preview:assembleDebug installed on this emulator.
# Fixture uses production OmaChatScreen/WebView; configuration handling matches OmaChatActivity.
fold open
rotate portrait
clearlog
shell am instrument -w dev.omalauncher.artifactpreview/.PreviewInstrumentation
log artifact IME Back and draft PASS
log artifact HTML JavaScript PASS
log artifact Files Source Preview PASS
log artifact focused fold cycles PASS
log artifact viewer Back and draft PASS
nolog artifact FAIL
# Physical emulator display transitions and screenshots reviewed separately from automated assertions.
fold folded
launch dev.omalauncher.artifactpreview/.PreviewActivity
# A new fixture launch has fictional, fresh thread metadata. Create its draft here.
tap ask soma
type Keep this draft
key BACK
expect Keep this draft
shot artifact-cover-chat
# The first Back after focusing the composer hides the IME; viewer Back must then return to the same draft.
tap listening-room.html
expect listening-room.html
expect [ source ]
shot artifact-cover-viewer
tap [ source ]
expect <!doctype html>
shot artifact-cover-source
tap [ files ]
expect From this conversation
tap interaction-notes.md
expect Close it to return to the same draft.
key BACK
expect Keep this draft
fold open
tap listening-room.html
expect [ expand ]
shot artifact-unfolded-preview
# A clicked HTML button has native WebView focus before the display is folded.
# Fold8 unfolded layout, measured from artifact-unfolded-preview: sample button in right pane.
# API37's uiautomator reconnect can omit WebView virtual nodes. The earlier instrumentation asserts JS;
# this real tap has a screenshot that must visibly say PLAYING / SIDE A before the walk counts.
tap 0.624 0.811
wait 500
shot artifact-interactive-html
# Folded, the viewer covers the chat with "← chat" to go back (artifact-panel mockup); unfolded it has close/expand.
fold folded
# The emulator's fold shows Android's "swipe up to continue" for a moment; the screenshot waits it out.
wait 2000
expect [ ← chat ]
absent [ expand ]
fold open
expect [ expand ]
tap [ close ]
expect Keep this draft
shot artifact-unfolded-chat-restored
# Regression: the list (now "artifacts · N", artifact-panel slice 1) must be discoverable in Phone B before it has outputs.
shell am force-stop dev.omalauncher.artifactpreview
shell am start -n dev.omalauncher.artifactpreview/.PreviewActivity --ez empty true
expect Phone B
expect [ artifacts · 0 ]
tap [ artifacts · 0 ]
expect No artifacts in this conversation yet.
shot artifact-phone-b-empty-files-unfolded
tap [ close ]
absent No artifacts in this conversation yet.
fold folded
wait 2000
expect [ artifacts · 0 ]
tap [ artifacts · 0 ]
expect No artifacts in this conversation yet.
expect [ close ]
shot artifact-phone-b-empty-files-cover
key BACK
absent No artifacts in this conversation yet.
expect [ artifacts · 0 ]
[phone] Open an output from an existing Mac Pro conversation: Preview loads through the authenticated runner, Source and Files work; Discuss adds context to the draft without sending.
[phone] Open an output from this MacBook conversation after its runner update; confirm on-demand file read and interactive HTML without an external app switch.
[phone] With a web page focused, physically fold/unfold three times. Chat and selected output remain usable; close/Back returns to the existing draft and reading position.
[phone] On cover, open the composer keyboard, press Back once to dismiss IME, then open an artifact and press Back: viewer closes, draft remains. Verify the Samsung IME and actual fold separately from emulator checks.
[phone] Soma Canvas in the panel (Boss, 2026-10-26: "default to opening it in the Soma chat panel"): tap a [Soma Canvas: Hunch](http://<canvas Mac>:5860/a/hunch) link in a reply. It opens in the artifact panel beside the chat, not Brave, and draws the Hunch board (not a white page: the page needs localStorage). Open the owner link once in the panel; after closing and reopening the panel, NEEDS YOU still shows and approving is offered.

# Artifact reply bridge: deferred until the native review UI has its Approved Canvas card.
[phone] Open an agent-made question HTML declaring soma-reply-to=phone:B. Choose options/Other and Submit: Soma shows the complete answer and Phone B in a native review; nothing reaches the agent before Send. Cancel preserves the form and sends nothing. Repeat and Send once; exactly one normal message reaches Phone B and appears in its chat.
[phone] Repeat with a known Mac thread key while its runner is reachable. Verify only that thread receives the exact previewed answer. Unknown recipients, a missing/duplicate meta declaration, subframe calls, script timers and live web pages cannot relay a message. A new artifact version invalidates an old review. Repeated Send cannot duplicate delivery.
